 reachable transport path to the non-voter, and insufficient successful voter confirmations after VerifyLeader is admitted.\",\n   \"assumptions\": [\n    \"The mixed configuration is committed before VerifyLeader is admitted.\",\n    \"The leader is still in Leader state when VerifyLeader is admitted.\",\n    \"The non-voter can answer the verification heartbeat successfully.\"\n   ],\n   \"excluded\": [\n    \"Log commit safety and election safety under voter-only quorums.\",\n    \"Callers that do not use VerifyLeader as a read or authority guard.\",\n    \"Transports that fabricate successful responses without delivering the RPC.\"\n   ],\n   \"parameters\": {\n    \"voter_count\": 3,\n    \"nonvoter_count\": 1,\n    \"quorum_size\": 2\n   }\n  },\n  \"description\": \"Measured violated comparison; current confirmation: False\",\n  \"assessment\": \"inconclusive\",\n  \"stale_reason\": null,\n  \"checker_id\": \"nonvoter_cannot_complete_verify_quorum\",\n  \"claim_version\": 1,\n  \"applicability\": \"current\"\n }\n]\n==== selections\n[\n {\n  \"operation_id\": \"b19ea898391f49e5afb8374add6f23dd\",\n  \"action\": \"check\",\n  \"rationale\": \"Execute a real four-node Raft cluster with a committed three-voter/one-non-voter configuration, partition the two non-leader voters, and observe whether VerifyLeader can be confirmed from the reachable non-voter despite the missing voter quorum.\",\n  \"feedback\": {},\n  \"map_updated\": false,\n  \"map_changes\": {},\n  \"accepted_versions\": {\n   \"audit_spec\": 0,\n   \"graph\": 1,\n   \"units\": {\n    \"unit-claim-verifyleader-voter-quorum-only\": 1\n   },\n   \"artifacts\": {\n    \"4d6db0cc9a4b4879b86886aeead58c33\": 1\n   }\n  },\n  \"candidate_ids\": [\n   \"fb5c370c7acf451584b6ba19cc294a9d\"\n  ]\n }\n]\n==== claims\n[\n {\n  \"id\": \"claim-verifyleader-voter-quorum-only\",\n  \"kind\": \"obligation\",\n  \"concern\": \"consensus_safety\",\n  \"description\": \"Whenever VerifyLeader completes successfully on a leader, the leader must have observed successful responses sufficient to meet the voter quorum of its latest configuration; confirmations from servers whose suffrage is not Voter must not contribute to that quorum.\",\n  \"scope\": {\n   \"description\": \"A leader with a committed configuration containing both voters and at least one non-voter, a reachable transport path to the non-voter, and insufficient successful voter confirmations after VerifyLeader is admitted.\",\n   \"assumptions\": [\n    \"The mixed configuration is committed before VerifyLeader is admitted.\",\n    \"The leader is still in Leader state when VerifyLeader is admitted.\",\n    \"The non-voter can answer the verification heartbeat successfully.\"\n   ],\n   \"excluded\": [\n    \"Log commit safety and election safety under voter-only quorums.\",\n    \"Callers that do not use VerifyLeader as a read or authority guard.\",\n    \"Transports that fabricate successful responses without delivering the RPC.\"\n   ],\n   \"parameters\": {\n    \"voter_count\": 3,\n    \"nonvoter_count\": 1,\n    \"quorum_size\": 2\n   }\n  },\n  \"source\": \"Candidate derived from attributed implementation responsibilities\",\n  \"source_ids\": [\n   \"src-api-verifyleader\",\n   \"src-suffrage\",\n   \"src-verifyleader\",\n   \"src-vote\",\n   \"src-notifyall\",\n   \"src-heartbeat\",\n   \"src-startstop\",\n   \"src-quorum\",\n   \"src-lease\"\n  ],\n  \"pending\": [],\n  \"assessment\": \"unassessed\",\n  \"candidate\": true,\n  \"grounding\": {\n   \"source_ids\": [\n    \"src-api-verifyleader\",\n    \"src-suffrage\",\n    \"src-verifyleader\",\n    \"src-vote\",\n    \"src-notifyall\",\n    \"src-heartbeat\",\n    \"src-startstop\",\n    \"src-quorum\",\n    \"src-lease\"\n   ],\n   \"expectation_ids\": [],\n   \"binding_ids\": [\n    \"bind-api-verifyleader\",\n    \"bind-suffrage\",\n    \"bind-verifyleader\",\n    \"bind-vote\",\n    \"bind-notifyall\",\n    \"bind-heartbeat\",\n    \"bind-startstop\",\n    \"bind-quorum\",\n    \"bind-lease\"\n   ],\n   \"derivation\": \"VerifyLeader is documented to ensure this peer is still leader and to prevent returning stale FSM data. The configuration contract distinguishes Voter from Nonvoter for elections and commitment. The implementation computes VerifyLeader's quorum from Voter entries only, but registers the verification request on every configured replication stream; a successful heartbeat to any stream calls notifyAll, whose true branch increments the same vote counter checked against the voter-sized quorum.\",\n   \"applicability\": \"A committed configuration contains at least one Voter, at least one Nonvoter, the non-voter is reachable, and the leader has fewer successful voter confirmations than its voter quorum after the VerifyLeader request is registered.\",\n   \"unresolved\": [\n    \"The observation covers one configuration shape and one transport schedule; it does not establish every possible cluster size or transport implementation.\"\n   ],\n   \"conflicts\": [\n    \"checkLeaderLease counts only Voter entries and can step the leader down on its own timer, but it does not gate the VerifyLeader completion observed here.\"\n   ],\n   \"alternatives\": [\n    \"A caller that ignores VerifyLeader is outside this obligation.\"\n   ]\n  },\n  \"version\": 1\n }\n]\n==== bindings\n[\n {\n  \"associations\": [\n   {\n    \"claim_id\": \"claim-verifyleader-voter-quorum-only\",\n    \"source_ids\": [\n     \"src-api-verifyleader\"\n    ],\n    \"rationale\": \"Public contract: VerifyLeader is used to ensure this peer is still leader and to prevent returning stale FSM data after leadership is lost.\"\n   }\n  ],\n  \"anchor\": {\n   \"source_ids\": [\n    \"src-api-verifyleader\"\n   ],\n   \"boundary_complete\": true,\n   \"kind\": \"declaration\",\n   \"material_id\": \"src-api-verifyleader\",\n   \"start_line\": 883,\n   \"end_line\": 883,\n   \"symbol\": \"VerifyLeader\"\n  },\n  \"material_id\": \"src-api-verifyleader\",\n  \"id\": \"bind-api-verifyleader\",\n  \"file\": \"api.go\",\n  \"symbol\": \"VerifyLeader\",\n  \"start_line\": 880,\n  \"end_line\": 893,\n  \"snapshot_id\": \"a1a939b7deaa4b84a668e3a1b36a3af7\",\n  \"content_digest\": \"499a72c01096912e85d16381f4640ac6d29f8c2b91cabbdae8530bdcbeb89a4a\",\n  \"basis\": \"agent_inference\",\n  \"description\": \"Public contract: VerifyLeader is used to ensure this peer is still leader and to prevent returning stale FSM data after leadership is lost.\",\n  \"pending\": [],\n  \"excerpt\": \"// VerifyLeader is used to ensure this peer is still the leader. It may be used\\n// to prevent returning stale data from the FSM after the peer has lost\\n// leadership.\\nfunc (r *Raft) VerifyLeader() Future {\\n\\tmetrics.IncrCounter([]string{\\\"raft\\\", \\\"verify_leader\\\"}, 1)\\n\\tverifyFuture := &verifyFuture{}\\n\\tverifyFuture.init()\\n\\tselect {\\n\\tcase <-r.shutdownCh:\\n\\t\\treturn errorFuture{ErrRaftShutdown}\\n\\tcase r.verifyCh <- verifyFuture:\\n\\t\\treturn verifyFuture\\n\\t}\\n}\",\n  \"version\": 1\n },\n {\n  \"associations\": [\n   {\n    \"claim_id\": \"claim-verifyleader-voter-quorum-only\",\n    \"source_ids\": [\n     \"src-suffrage\"\n    ],\n    \"rationale\": \"Suffrage contract: Voter is counted for elections and commitment; Nonvoter is not considered for elections or commitment purposes.\"\n   }\n  ],\n  \"anchor\": {\n   \"source_ids\": [\n    \"src-suffrage\"\n   ],\n   \"boundary_complete\": true,\n   \"kind\": \"declaration\",\n   \"material_id\": \"src-suffrage\",\n   \"start_line\": 9,\n   \"end_line\": 9,\n   \"symbol\": \"ServerSuffrage\"\n  },\n  \"material_id\": \"src-suffrage\",\n  \"id\": \"bind-suffrage\",\n  \"file\": \"configuration.go\",\n  \"symbol\": \"ServerSuffrage\",\n  \"start_line\": 9,\n  \"end_line\": 9,\n  \"snapshot_id\": \"a1a939b7deaa4b84a668e3a1b36a3af7\",\n  \"content_digest\": \"7e3e1e0a708f3f3b17691549962c94d78955a840922fc0f42867c515cd27ec66\",\n  \"basis\": \"agent_inference\",\n  \"description\": \"Suffrage contract: Voter is counted for elections and commitment; Nonvoter is not considered for elections or commitment purposes.\",\n  \"pending\": [],\n  \"excerpt\": \"type ServerSuffrage int\",\n  \"version\": 1\n },\n {\n  \"associations\": [\n   {\n    \"claim_id\": \"claim-verifyleader-voter-quorum-only\",\n    \"source_ids\": [\n     \"src-verifyleader\"\n    ],\n    \"rationale\": \"Sets the verify quorum from quorumSize but registers the request on every replication state.\"\n   }\n  ],\n  \"anchor\": {\n   \"source_ids\": [\n    \"src-verifyleader\"\n   ],\n   \"boundary_complete\": true,\n   \"kind\": \"declaration\",\n   \"material_id\": \"src-verifyleader\",\n   \"start_line\": 965,\n   \"end_line\": 965,\n   \"symbol\": \"verifyLeader\"\n  },\n  \"material_id\": \"src-verifyleader\",\n  \"id\": \"bind-verifyleader\",\n  \"file\": \"raft.go\",\n  \"symbol\": \"verifyLeader\",\n  \"start_line\": 963,\n  \"end_line\": 987,\n  \"snapshot_id\": \"a1a939b7deaa4b84a668e3a1b36a3af7\",\n  \"content_digest\": \"54d43df5197fd71cd0f6ae4eee1ba28efb139a5223eb14b756c606bdb0b8a800\",\n  \"basis\": \"agent_inference\",\n  \"description\": \"Sets the verify quorum from quorumSize but registers the request on every replication state.\",\n  \"pending\": [],\n  \"excerpt\": \"// verifyLeader must be called from the main thread for safety.\\n// Causes the followers to attempt an immediate heartbeat.\\nfunc (r *Raft) verifyLeader(v *verifyFuture) {\\n\\t// Current leader always votes for self\\n\\tv.votes = 1\\n\\n\\t// Set the quorum size, hot-path for single node\\n\\tv.quorumSize = r.quorumSize()\\n\\tif v.quorumSize == 1 {\\n\\t\\tv.respond(nil)\\n\\t\\treturn\\n\\t}\\n\\n\\t// Track this request\\n\\tv.notifyCh = r.verifyCh\\n\\tr.leaderState.notify[v] = struct{}{}\\n\\n\\t// Trigger immediate heartbeats\\n\\tfor _, repl := range r.leaderState.replState {\\n\\t\\trepl.notifyLock.Lock()\\n\\t\\trepl.notify[v] = struct{}{}\\n\\t\\trepl.notifyLock.Unlock()\\n\\t\\tasyncNotifyCh(repl.notifyCh)\\n\\t}\\n}\",\n  \"version\": 1\n },\n {\n  \"associations\": [\n   {\n    \"claim_id\": \"claim-verifyleader-voter-quorum-only\",\n    \"source_ids\": [\n     \"src-vote\"\n    ],\n    \"rationale\": \"Increments one shared vote count on a true notification and completes when it reaches quorumSize.\"\n   }\n  ],\n  \"anchor\": {\n   \"source_ids\": [\n    \"src-vote\"\n   ],\n   \"boundary_complete\": false,\n   \"kind\": \"declaration\",\n   \"material_id\": \"src-vote\",\n   \"start_line\": 274,\n   \"end_line\": 274,\n   \"symbol\": \"vote\"\n  },\n  \"material_id\": \"src-vote\",\n  \"id\": \"bind-vote\",\n  \"file\": \"future.go\",\n  \"symbol\": \"vote\",\n  \"start_line\": 272,\n  \"end_line\": 292,\n  \"snapshot_id\": \"a1a939b7deaa4b84a668e3a1b36a3af7\",\n  \"content_digest\": \"e3775d16c6cb24f9c9572ce452c27e87fcbf4b24baf666d14e838cc4b571ae9c\",\n  \"basis\": \"agent_inference\",\n  \"description\": \"Increments one shared vote count on a true notification and completes when it reaches quorumSize.\",\n  \"pending\": [],\n  \"excerpt\": \"// vote is used to respond to a verifyFuture.\\n// This may block when responding on the notifyCh.\\nfunc (v *verifyFuture) vote(leader bool) {\\n\\tv.voteLock.Lock()\\n\\tdefer v.voteLock.Unlock()\\n\\n\\t// Guard against having notified already\\n\\tif v.notifyCh == nil {\\n\\t\\treturn\\n\\t}\\n\\n\\tif leader {\\n\\t\\tv.votes++\\n\\t\\tif v.votes >= v.quorumSize {\\n\\t\\t\\tv.notifyCh <- v\\n\\t\\t\\tv.notifyCh = nil\\n\\t\\t}\\n\\t} else {\\n\\t\\tv.notifyCh <- v\\n\\t\\tv.notifyCh = nil\\n\\t}\",\n  \"version\": 1\n },\n {\n  \"associations\": [\n   {\n    \"claim_id\": \"claim-verifyleader-voter-quorum-only\",\n    \"source_ids\": [\n     \"src-notifyall\"\n    ],\n    \"rationale\": \"Delivers a leader=true notification to all waiters associated with this replication stream.\"\n   }\n  ],\n  \"anchor\": {\n   \"source_ids\": [\n    \"src-notifyall\"\n   ],\n   \"boundary_complete\": true,\n   \"kind\": \"declaration\",\n   \"material_id\": \"src-notifyall\",\n   \"start_line\": 100,\n   \"end_line\": 100,\n   \"symbol\": \"notifyAll\"\n  },\n  \"material_id\": \"src-notifyall\",\n  \"id\": \"bind-notifyall\",\n  \"file\": \"replication.go\",\n  \"symbol\": \"notifyAll\",\n  \"start_line\": 98,\n  \"end_line\": 111,\n  \"snapshot_id\": \"a1a939b7deaa4b84a668e3a1b36a3af7\",\n  \"content_digest\": \"24106024107950339bd30fc4e24a0b4a0a97a1c0e01aa7b31bedf4a2ad30b054\",\n  \"basis\": \"agent_inference\",\n  \"description\": \"Delivers a leader=true notification to all waiters associated with this replication stream.\",\n  \"pending\": [],\n  \"excerpt\": \"// notifyAll is used to notify all the waiting verify futures\\n// if the follower believes we are still the leader.\\nfunc (s *followerReplication) notifyAll(leader bool) {\\n\\t// Clear the waiting notifies minimizing lock time\\n\\ts.notifyLock.Lock()\\n\\tn := s.notify\\n\\ts.notify = make(map[*verifyFuture]struct{})\\n\\ts.notifyLock.Unlock()\\n\\n\\t// Submit our votes\\n\\tfor v := range n {\\n\\t\\tv.vote(leader)\\n\\t}\\n}\",\n  \"version\": 1\n },\n {\n  \"associations\": [\n   {\n    \"claim_id\": \"claim-verifyleader-voter-quorum-only\",\n    \"source_ids\": [\n     \"src-heartbeat\"\n    ],\n    \"rationale\": \"A successful heartbeat to any configured peer calls notifyAll(resp.Success).\"\n   }\n  ],\n  \"anchor\": {\n   \"source_ids\": [\n    \"src-heartbeat\"\n   ],\n   \"boundary_complete\": false,\n   \"kind\": \"declaration\",\n   \"material_id\": \"src-heartbeat\",\n   \"start_line\": 388,\n   \"end_line\": 388,\n   \"symbol\": \"heartbeat\"\n  },\n  \"material_id\": \"src-heartbeat\",\n  \"id\": \"bind-heartbeat\",\n  \"file\": \"replication.go\",\n  \"symbol\": \"heartbeat\",\n  \"start_line\": 385,\n  \"end_line\": 438,\n  \"snapshot_id\": \"a1a939b7deaa4b84a668e3a1b36a3af7\",\n  \"content_digest\": \"24106024107950339bd30fc4e24a0b4a0a97a1c0e01aa7b31bedf4a2ad30b054\",\n  \"basis\": \"agent_inference\",\n  \"description\": \"A successful heartbeat to any configured peer calls notifyAll(resp.Success).\",\n  \"pending\": [],\n  \"excerpt\": \"// heartbeat is used to periodically invoke AppendEntries on a peer\\n// to ensure they don't time out. This is done async of replicate(),\\n// since that routine could potentially be blocked on disk IO.\\nfunc (r *Raft) heartbeat(s *followerReplication, stopCh chan struct{}) {\\n\\tvar failures uint64\\n\\treq := AppendEntriesRequest{\\n\\t\\tRPCHeader: r.getRPCHeader(),\\n\\t\\tTerm:      s.currentTerm,\\n\\t\\t// this is needed for retro compatibility, before RPCHeader.Addr was added\\n\\t\\tLeader: r.trans.EncodePeer(r.localID, r.localAddr),\\n\\t}\\n\\n\\tvar resp AppendEntriesResponse\\n\\tfor {\\n\\t\\t// Wait for the next heartbeat interval or forced notify\\n\\t\\tselect {\\n\\t\\tcase <-s.notifyCh:\\n\\t\\tcase <-randomTimeout(r.config().HeartbeatTimeout / 10):\\n\\t\\tcase <-stopCh:\\n\\t\\t\\treturn\\n\\t\\t}\\n\\n\\t\\ts.peerLock.RLock()\\n\\t\\tpeer := s.peer\\n\\t\\ts.peerLock.RUnlock()\\n\\n\\t\\tstart := time.Now()\\n\\t\\tif err := r.trans.AppendEntries(peer.ID, peer.Address, &req, &resp); err != nil {\\n\\t\\t\\tnextBackoffTime := cappedExponentialBackoff(failureWait, failures, maxFailureScale, r.config().HeartbeatTimeout/2)\\n\\t\\t\\tr.logger.Error(\\\"failed to heartbeat to\\\", \\\"peer\\\", peer.Address, \\\"backoff time\\\",\\n\\t\\t\\t\\tnextBackoffTime, \\\"error\\\", err)\\n\\t\\t\\tr.observe(FailedHeartbeatObservation{PeerID: peer.ID, LastContact: s.LastContact()})\\n\\t\\t\\tfailures++\\n\\t\\t\\tselect {\\n\\t\\t\\tcase <-time.After(nextBackoffTime):\\n\\t\\t\\tcase <-stopCh:\\n\\t\\t\\t\\treturn\\n\\t\\t\\t}\\n\\t\\t} else {\\n\\t\\t\\tif failures > 0 {\\n\\t\\t\\t\\tr.observe(ResumedHeartbeatObservation{PeerID: peer.ID})\\n\\t\\t\\t}\\n\\t\\t\\ts.setLastContact()\\n\\t\\t\\tfailures = 0\\n\\t\\t\\tlabels := []metrics.Label{{Name: \\\"peer_id\\\", Value: string(peer.ID)}}\\n\\t\\t\\tmetrics.MeasureSinceWithLabels([]string{\\\"raft\\\", \\\"replication\\\", \\\"heartbeat\\\"}, start, labels)\\n\\n\\t\\t\\tif !r.noLegacyTelemetry {\\n\\t\\t\\t\\t// Duplicated information. Kept for backward compatibility.\\n\\t\\t\\t\\tmetrics.MeasureSince([]string{\\\"raft\\\", \\\"replication\\\", \\\"heartbeat\\\", string(peer.ID)}, start)\\n\\t\\t\\t}\\n\\n\\t\\t\\ts.notifyAll(resp.Success)\\n\\t\\t}\",\n  \"version\": 1\n },\n {\n  \"associations\": [\n   {\n    \"claim_id\": \"claim-verifyleader-voter-quorum-only\",\n    \"source_ids\": [\n     \"src-startstop\"\n    ],\n    \"rationale\": \"Creates replication state for every configured server other than the local server without filtering out non-voters.\"\n   }\n  ],\n  \"anchor\": {\n   \"source_ids\": [\n    \"src-startstop\"\n   ],\n   \"boundary_complete\": true,\n   \"kind\": \"declaration\",\n   \"material_id\": \"src-startstop\",\n   \"start_line\": 582,\n   \"end_line\": 582,\n   \"symbol\": \"startStopReplication\"\n  },\n  \"material_id\": \"src-startstop\",\n  \"id\": \"bind-startstop\",\n  \"file\": \"raft.go\",\n  \"symbol\": \"startStopReplication\",\n  \"start_line\": 582,\n  \"end_line\": 645,\n  \"snapshot_id\": \"a1a939b7deaa4b84a668e3a1b36a3af7\",\n  \"content_digest\": \"54d43df5197fd71cd0f6ae4eee1ba28efb139a5223eb14b756c606bdb0b8a800\",\n  \"basis\": \"agent_inference\",\n  \"description\": \"Creates replication state for every configured server other than the local server without filtering out non-voters.\",\n  \"pending\": [],\n  \"excerpt\": \"func (r *Raft) startStopReplication() {\\n\\tinConfig := make(map[ServerID]bool, len(r.configurations.latest.Servers))\\n\\tlastIdx := r.getLastIndex()\\n\\n\\t// Start replication goroutines that need starting\\n\\tfor _, server := range r.configurations.latest.Servers {\\n\\t\\tif server.ID == r.localID {\\n\\t\\t\\tcontinue\\n\\t\\t}\\n\\n\\t\\tinConfig[server.ID] = true\\n\\n\\t\\ts, ok := r.leaderState.replState[server.ID]\\n\\t\\tif !ok {\\n\\t\\t\\tr.logger.Info(\\\"added peer, starting replication\\\", \\\"peer\\\", server.ID)\\n\\t\\t\\ts = &followerReplication{\\n\\t\\t\\t\\tpeer:                server,\\n\\t\\t\\t\\tcommitment:          r.leaderState.commitment,\\n\\t\\t\\t\\tstopCh:              make(chan uint64, 1),\\n\\t\\t\\t\\ttriggerCh:           make(chan struct{}, 1),\\n\\t\\t\\t\\ttriggerDeferErrorCh: make(chan *deferError, 1),\\n\\t\\t\\t\\tcurrentTerm:         r.getCurrentTerm(),\\n\\t\\t\\t\\tnextIndex:           lastIdx + 1,\\n\\t\\t\\t\\tlastContact:         time.Now(),\\n\\t\\t\\t\\tnotify:              make(map[*verifyFuture]struct{}),\\n\\t\\t\\t\\tnotifyCh:            make(chan struct{}, 1),\\n\\t\\t\\t\\tstepDown:            r.leaderState.stepDown,\\n\\t\\t\\t}\\n\\n\\t\\t\\tr.leaderState.replState[server.ID] = s\\n\\t\\t\\tr.goFunc(func() { r.replicate(s) })\\n\\t\\t\\tasyncNotifyCh(s.triggerCh)\\n\\t\\t\\tr.observe(PeerObservation{Peer: server, Removed: false})\\n\\t\\t} else if ok {\\n\\n\\t\\t\\ts.peerLock.RLock()\\n\\t\\t\\tpeer := s.peer\\n\\t\\t\\ts.peerLock.RUnlock()\\n\\n\\t\\t\\tif peer.Address != server.Address {\\n\\t\\t\\t\\tr.logger.Info(\\\"updating peer\\\", \\\"peer\\\", server.ID)\\n\\t\\t\\t\\ts.peerLock.Lock()\\n\\t\\t\\t\\ts.peer = server\\n\\t\\t\\t\\ts.peerLock.Unlock()\\n\\t\\t\\t}\\n\\t\\t}\\n\\t}\\n\\n\\t// Stop replication goroutines that need stopping\\n\\tfor serverID, repl := range r.leaderState.replState {\\n\\t\\tif inConfig[serverID] {\\n\\t\\t\\tcontinue\\n\\t\\t}\\n\\t\\t// Replicate up to lastIdx and stop\\n\\t\\tr.logger.Info(\\\"removed peer, stopping replication\\\", \\\"peer\\\", serverID, \\\"last-index\\\", lastIdx)\\n\\t\\trepl.stopCh <- lastIdx\\n\\t\\tclose(repl.stopCh)\\n\\t\\tdelete(r.leaderState.replState, serverID)\\n\\t\\tr.observe(PeerObservation{Peer: repl.peer, Removed: true})\\n\\t}\\n\\n\\t// Update peers metric\\n\\tmetrics.SetGauge([]string{\\\"raft\\\", \\\"peers\\\"}, float32(len(r.configurations.latest.Servers)))\\n}\",\n  \"version\": 1\n },\n {\n  \"associations\": [\n   {\n    \"claim_id\": \"claim-verifyleader-voter-quorum-only\",\n    \"source_ids\": [\n     \"src-quorum\"\n    ],\n    \"rationale\": \"Computes quorum solely from Voter entries in the latest configuration.\"\n   }\n  ],\n  \"anchor\": {\n   \"source_ids\": [\n    \"src-quorum\"\n   ],\n   \"boundary_complete\": false,\n   \"kind\": \"declaration\",\n   \"material_id\": \"src-quorum\",\n   \"start_line\": 1086,\n   \"end_line\": 1086,\n   \"symbol\": \"quorumSize\"\n  },\n  \"material_id\": \"src-quorum\",\n  \"id\": \"bind-quorum\",\n  \"file\": \"raft.go\",\n  \"symbol\": \"quorumSize\",\n  \"start_line\": 1083,\n  \"end_line\": 1093,\n  \"snapshot_id\": \"a1a939b7deaa4b84a668e3a1b36a3af7\",\n  \"content_digest\": \"54d43df5197fd71cd0f6ae4eee1ba28efb139a5223eb14b756c606bdb0b8a800\",\n  \"basis\": \"agent_inference\",\n  \"description\": \"Computes quorum solely from Voter entries in the latest configuration.\",\n  \"pending\": [],\n  \"excerpt\": \"// quorumSize is used to return the quorum size. This must only be called on\\n// the main thread.\\n// TODO: revisit usage\\nfunc (r *Raft) quorumSize() int {\\n\\tvoters := 0\\n\\tfor _, server := range r.configurations.latest.Servers {\\n\\t\\tif server.Suffrage == Voter {\\n\\t\\t\\tvoters++\\n\\t\\t}\\n\\t}\\n\\treturn voters/2 + 1\",\n  \"version\": 1\n },\n {\n  \"associations\": [\n   {\n    \"claim_id\": \"claim-verifyleader-voter-quorum-only\",\n    \"source_ids\": [\n     \"src-lease\"\n    ],\n    \"rationale\": \"The lease check counts only Voter entries, providing a contrast to VerifyLeader's all-stream registration.\"\n   }\n  ],\n  \"anchor\": {\n   \"source_ids\": [\n    \"src-lease\"\n   ],\n   \"boundary_complete\": true,\n   \"kind\": \"declaration\",\n   \"material_id\": \"src-lease\",\n   \"start_line\": 1036,\n   \"end_line\": 1036,\n   \"symbol\": \"checkLeaderLease\"\n  },\n  \"material_id\": \"src-lease\",\n  \"id\": \"bind-lease\",\n  \"file\": \"raft.go\",\n  \"symbol\": \"checkLeaderLease\",\n  \"start_line\": 1032,\n  \"end_line\": 1081,\n  \"snapshot_id\": \"a1a939b7deaa4b84a668e3a1b36a3af7\",\n  \"content_digest\": \"54d43df5197fd71cd0f6ae4eee1ba28efb139a5223eb14b756c606bdb0b8a800\",\n  \"basis\": \"agent_inference\",\n  \"description\": \"The lease check counts only Voter entries, providing a contrast to VerifyLeader's all-stream registration.\",\n  \"pending\": [],\n  \"excerpt\": \"// checkLeaderLease is used to check if we can contact a quorum of nodes\\n// within the last leader lease interval. If not, we need to step down,\\n// as we may have lost connectivity. Returns the maximum duration without\\n// contact. This must only be called from the main thread.\\nfunc (r *Raft) checkLeaderLease() time.Duration {\\n\\t// Track contacted nodes, we can always contact ourself\\n\\tcontacted := 0\\n\\n\\t// Store lease timeout for this one check invocation as we need to refer to it\\n\\t// in the loop and would be confusing if it ever becomes reloadable and\\n\\t// changes between iterations below.\\n\\tleaseTimeout := r.config().LeaderLeaseTimeout\\n\\n\\t// Check each follower\\n\\tvar maxDiff time.Duration\\n\\tnow := time.Now()\\n\\tfor _, server := range r.configurations.latest.Servers {\\n\\t\\tif server.Suffrage == Voter {\\n\\t\\t\\tif server.ID == r.localID {\\n\\t\\t\\t\\tcontacted++\\n\\t\\t\\t\\tcontinue\\n\\t\\t\\t}\\n\\t\\t\\tf := r.leaderState.replState[server.ID]\\n\\t\\t\\tdiff := now.Sub(f.LastContact())\\n\\t\\t\\tif diff <= leaseTimeout {\\n\\t\\t\\t\\tcontacted++\\n\\t\\t\\t\\tif diff > maxDiff {\\n\\t\\t\\t\\t\\tmaxDiff = diff\\n\\t\\t\\t\\t}\\n\\t\\t\\t} else {\\n\\t\\t\\t\\t// Log at least once at high value, then debug. Otherwise it gets very verbose.\\n\\t\\t\\t\\tif diff <= 3*leaseTimeout {\\n\\t\\t\\t\\t\\tr.logger.Warn(\\\"failed to contact\\\", \\\"server-id\\\", server.ID, \\\"time\\\", diff)\\n\\t\\t\\t\\t} else {\\n\\t\\t\\t\\t\\tr.logger.Debug(\\\"failed to contact\\\", \\\"server-id\\\", server.ID, \\\"time\\\", diff)\\n\\t\\t\\t\\t}\\n\\t\\t\\t}\\n\\t\\t\\tmetrics.AddSample([]string{\\\"raft\\\", \\\"leader\\\", \\\"lastContact\\\"}, float32(diff/time.Millisecond))\\n\\t\\t}\\n\\t}\\n\\n\\t// Verify we can contact a quorum\\n\\tquorum := r.quorumSize()\\n\\tif contacted < quorum {\\n\\t\\tr.logger.Warn(\\\"failed to contact quorum of nodes, stepping down\\\")\\n\\t\\tr.setState(Follower)\\n\\t\\tmetrics.IncrCounter([]string{\\\"raft\\\", \\\"transition\\\", \\\"leader_lease_timeout\\\"}, 1)\\n\\t}\\n\\treturn maxDiff\\n}\",\n  \"version\": 1\n }\n]\n==== units\n[\n {\n  \"id\": \"unit-claim-verifyleader-voter-quorum-only\",\n  \"candidate_id\": \"fb5c370c7acf451584b6ba19cc294a9d\",\n  \"obligation_ids\": [\n   \"claim-verifyleader-voter-quorum-only\"\n  ],\n  \"binding_ids\": [\n   \"bind-api-verifyleader\",\n   \"bind-suffrage\",\n   \"bind-verifyleader\",\n   \"bind-vote\",\n   \"bind-notifyall\",\n   \"bind-heartbeat\",\n   \"bind-startstop\",\n   \"bind-quorum\",\n   \"bind-lease\"\n  ],\n  \"relation_ids\": [],\n  \"scope\": {\n   \"description\": \"A leader with a committed configuration containing both voters and at least one non-voter, a reachable transport path to the non-voter, and insufficient successful voter confirmations after VerifyLeader is admitted.\",\n   \"assumptions\": [\n    \"The mixed configuration is committed before VerifyLeader is admitted.\",\n    \"The leader is still in Leader state when VerifyLeader is admitted.\",\n    \"The non-voter can answer the verification heartbeat successfully.\"\n   ],\n   \"excluded\": [\n    \"Log commit safety and election safety under voter-only quorums.\",\n    \"Callers that do not use VerifyLeader as a read or authority guard.\",\n    \"Transports that fabricate successful responses without delivering the RPC.\"\n   ],\n   \"parameters\": {\n    \"voter_count\": 3,\n    \"nonvoter_count\": 1,\n    \"quorum_size\": 2\n   }\n  },\n  \"rationale\": \"The public VerifyLeader contract and the suffrage contract jointly require voter-quorum confirmation. The implementation appears to register every replication stream, including non-voters, on the same quorum-sized vote counter.\",\n  \"status\": \"partial\",\n  \"previous_id\": null,\n  \"version\": 1,\n  \"boundary_changes\": [],\n  \"obligation_checks\": {\n   \"claim-verifyleader-voter-quorum-only\": [\n    \"3c9d7e6ae7a04f4f9ce7a782e755960a\"\n   ]\n  },\n  \"remaining_obligation_ids\": [\n   \"claim-verifyleader-voter-quorum-only\"\n  ],\n  \"recheck_reasons\": [],\n  \"audit_question\": {\n   \"audit_spec_version\": null,\n   \"disposition\": \"concrete_suspicion\",\n   \"preferred_check\": \"direct_test\",\n   \"question\": \"Can a leader that cannot reach a quorum of its configured voters still receive a successful VerifyLeader result because a configured non-voter answers the verification heartbeat?\",\n   \"importance\": \"VerifyLeader is documented as a guard against returning stale FSM data after leadership is lost; counting non-voter confirmations can let a separated leader confirm authority.\",\n   \"source_ids\": [\n    \"src-api-verifyleader\",\n    \"src-suffrage\",\n    \"src-verifyleader\",\n    \"src-vote\",\n    \"src-notifyall\",\n    \"src-heartbeat\",\n    \"src-startstop\",\n    \"src-quorum\",\n    \"src-lease\"\n   ],\n   \"participants\": [],\n   \"objects\": [\n    \"VerifyLeader quorum\",\n    \"leader replication state\",\n    \"non-voter suffrage\"\n   ],\n   \"contexts\": [\n    \"leader with a committed mixed-voter configuration and a partitioned voter quorum\"\n   ],\n   \"event_paths\": [\n    \"VerifyLeader -> verifyCh -> per-replication notify -> verification heartbeat -> notifyAll -> shared vote comparison\"\n   ],\n   \"activity_classes\": [],\n   \"behavior_ids\": [],\n   \"fact_ids\": [],\n   \"supporting_behavior_ids\": {},\n   \"obligation_relation_kind\": null,\n   \"counterevidence\": [\n    \"checkLeaderLease counts only Voter entries and can step the leader down later, but that separate timer does not mediate this VerifyLeader completion.\"\n   ],\n   \"unknowns\": [\n    \"Whether the surrounding deployment uses VerifyLeader as a linearizable-read guard.\",\n    \"How long a caller may act on a false confirmation before the separate lease check fires.\"\n   ],\n   \"trigger_rationale\": \"The source binds the documented stale-read guard and the suffrage distinction directly to the observed VerifyLeader completion path.\"\n  },\n  \"coverage_limitations\": [\n   \"Bounded direct comparison completed; local attribution remains pending: Direct oracle correspondence is unreviewed; Open review issue 9958e6a6c00b4d34acdbed54ba0a2d3d [src-api-verifyleader,src-suffrage,src-verifyleader,src-vote,src-notifyall,src-heartbeat,src-startstop,src-quorum,src-lease]: checkLeaderLease counts only Voter entries and can step the leader down on its own timer, but it does not gate the VerifyLeader completion observed here.; Open review issue 4311049142984708b86a1e4b44b2f74a [src-api-verifyleader,src-suffrage,src-verifyleader,src-vote,src-notifyall,src-heartbeat,src-startstop,src-quorum,src-lease]: The observation covers one configuration shape and one transport schedule; it does not establish every possible cluster size or transport implementation.; Open review issue e7ff46ef09484db8807fadc79c10fe4d [src-api-verifyleader,src-suffrage,src-verifyleader,src-vote,src-notifyall,src-heartbeat,src-startstop,src-quorum,src-lease]: checkLeaderLease counts only Voter entries and can step the leader down later, but it is a separate timer-driven check and does not mediate this VerifyLeader completion.; Open review issue 61beb51e6fe54d67b47e58f129e6a9e4 [src-api-verifyleader,src-suffrage,src-verifyleader,src-vote,src-notifyall,src-heartbeat,src-startstop,src-quorum,src-lease]: The check observes one configuration shape and one transport timing; it does not establish behavior for every possible configuration size or transport implementation.\"\n  ]\n }\n]\n==== question_candidates\n[\n {\n  \"version\": 1,\n  \"id\": \"fb5c370c7acf451584b6ba19cc294a9d\",\n  \"question\": {\n   \"audit_spec_version\": null,\n   \"disposition\": \"concrete_suspicion\",\n   \"preferred_check\": \"direct_test\",\n   \"question\": \"Can a leader that cannot reach a quorum of its configured voters still receive a successful VerifyLeader result because a configured non-voter answers the verification heartbeat?\",\n   \"importance\": \"VerifyLeader is documented as a guard against returning stale FSM data after leadership is lost; counting non-voter confirmations can let a separated leader confirm authority.\",\n   \"source_ids\": [\n    \"src-api-verifyleader\",\n    \"src-suffrage\",\n    \"src-verifyleader\",\n    \"src-vote\",\n    \"src-notifyall\",\n    \"src-heartbeat\",\n    \"src-startstop\",\n    \"src-quorum\",\n    \"src-lease\"\n   ],\n   \"participants\": [],\n   \"objects\": [\n    \"VerifyLeader quorum\",\n    \"leader replication state\",\n    \"non-voter suffrage\"\n   ],\n   \"contexts\": [\n    \"leader with a committed mixed-voter configuration and a partitioned voter quorum\"\n   ],\n   \"event_paths\": [\n    \"VerifyLeader -> verifyCh -> per-replication notify -> verification heartbeat -> notifyAll -> shared vote comparison\"\n   ],\n   \"activity_classes\": [],\n   \"behavior_ids\": [],\n   \"fact_ids\": [],\n   \"supporting_behavior_ids\": {},\n   \"obligation_relation_kind\": null,\n   \"counterevidence\": [\n    \"checkLeaderLease counts only Voter entries and can step the leader down later, but that separate timer does not mediate this VerifyLeader completion.\"\n   ],\n   \"unknowns\": [\n    \"Whether the surrounding deployment uses VerifyLeader as a linearizable-read guard.\",\n    \"How long a caller may act on a false confirmation before the separate lease check fires.\"\n   ],\n   \"trigger_rationale\": \"The source binds the documented stale-read guard and the suffrage distinction directly to the observed VerifyLeader completion path.\"\n  },\n  \"history\": [],\n  \"check_ids\": [\n   \"b19ea898391f49e5afb8374add6f23dd\"\n  ],\n  \"status\": \"escalated\",\n  \"parent_candidate_id\": null,\n  \"stop_reason\": \"The public VerifyLeader contract and the suffrage contract jointly require voter-quorum confirmation. The implementation appears to register every replication stream, including non-voters, on the same quorum-sized vote counter.\",\n  \"resume_conditions\": [],\n  \"obligation_id\": \"claim-verifyleader-voter-quorum-only\"\n }\n]\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
